    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **54 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, returning both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getMembershipPoints()` and rewrote `getMembershipLevel()`:\n- `getMembershipPoints()`: starts at 0; +2 email present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; +2 for a household of 3+ (`householdMemberCount >= 3`); +3 for tenure over 365 days.\n- `getMembershipLevel()`: derives from points \u2014 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated the `membershipLevel` description/constraints (max now 4). Since the DTO is generated from this spec and the MapStruct mapper matches by getter name, both fields flow into `OwnerDto` automatically \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\nThe tenure factor (+3) remains the only route to 6+ points, so a newly created owner (zero tenure) still tops out at 5 points / level 3, which the existing tenure-cap tests confirm.",
