    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is every validation and side-effect for `POST /api/owners`, in pipeline order.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **`authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded; a caller without that role is rejected (403 via `AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` (binds `@RequestBody`, no `@Valid`)\nThis is the single body-reader. In order inside the method:\n- Normalizes `address` first (`AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n- **Required-field check** on `firstName`, `lastName`, the *normalized* `address`, `city`, `telephone` \u2014 any blank/missing ones are collected and thrown together as `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, `errors` array).\n- Stores the normalized address back on the body.\n- Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`TelephoneE164`: strip separators; keep a leading `+` country code or assume `+61` dropping one leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61` needs exactly 9 national digits, `+1` exactly 10). If it can't form a valid E.164 \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n- Normalizes `email` (`OwnerEmail`): optional; if present must match the syntactic pattern and must **not** be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400); stored lower-cased.\n- **Side-effect:** publishes the mutated/normalized body for later steps.\n\n## 2. `ValidatePostcode`\n- Postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits, and when `city` maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must be in range; unknown city accepts any 4 digits. Else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n## 3. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n- If a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n## 4. `EnsureCityCapacity` *(transaction begins here)*\n- Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409). Count excludes the new owner.\n\n## 5. `ResolveRegistrationDate`\n- **Side-effect:** computes the effective registration date = supplied date, or today if absent, then rolls weekends forward to Monday (`BusinessDay`); publishes it for downstream use.\n\n## 6. `EnsureDailyCapacity`\n- Counts existing owners whose stored registration date equals that effective business-day date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (429).\n\n## 7. `BuildOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and sets its `registrationDate` to the effective business-day date.\n\n## 8. `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (postcode empty when absent).\n\n## 9. `EnsureUniqueHousehold`\n- If `sharesHousehold` is true, skip. Otherwise, if any existing owner already has the same `householdId` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n\n## 10. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- If any existing owner has the same full `identityKey` (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 11. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- If `sharesHousehold` true, or postcode null, skip. Otherwise, if an existing owner matches (same last name case-insensitive, same postcode, **different** telephone), **side-effect:** set `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching owner id.\n\n## 12. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`\n- **Side-effect:** set `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` + 1 (1 if no household id).\n\n## 13. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where region is derived (postcode then city) and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256(`telephone + lastName`).\n\n## 14. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** set `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n\n## 15. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner (`ownerRepository.save`), assigning its id.\n\n## 16. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** logs an `AUDIT` line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n## 17. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already have today's business-day registration date, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Notes:**\n- All steps from #4 onward run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the write commits once at the end.\n- Body binding is intentionally without `@Valid`, so the only field validation is the explicit checks above \u2014 there is no bean-validation/`MethodArgumentNotValidException` path here.\n- Any thrown exception is handled by the matching YAML under `officefloor/escalation/`, giving the status codes noted."
